  "candidate": "Single workflow coordinator and native completion notifications",
  "candidate_guidance_patch": "diff --git a/docs/native-review.md b/docs/native-review.md\nindex 9f75cd2..203d783 100644\n--- a/docs/native-review.md\n+++ b/docs/native-review.md\n@@ -4,6 +4,13 @@ Use the host's native agent tools to invoke selected reviewer skills. A complete\n \n ## Launch and wait\n \n+Keep one workflow coordinator for the run. Invoke the selected skills directly;\n+do not add relay coordinators or agents that only repeat status. Prefer native\n+completion notifications to repeated status requests or agent messages. When\n+observation is necessary, wait on the saved handle and retain it across timeouts\n+and interruptions. Use the existing CI observer for CI. A timeout or missing\n+notification never proves a child stopped or succeeded.\n+\n 1. Resolve the skill and pin task inputs before launch. Prepare immutable context and output paths outside the source checkout. Supply the exact task, pinned source, original guidance, resolved resources, permitted actions and required completion report. Keep source inspection read-only. The skill manages its private state and lifecycle.\n    Include the complete [preference handoff](preferences.md#workflow-handoffs-and-reuse), retaining matched paths and conditional decisions. Reviewers and finding verifiers apply records only within that scope and request refreshed selection before expanding paths.\n 2. After `start-batch` returns `invoke`, launch the reviewer with native tools. Save its handle with the task key and claim id in private operational progress, outside fingerprinted inputs. Let the skill manage its internal passes and required resources.\ndiff --git a/runtime/pr-iter.md b/runtime/pr-iter.md\nindex 9e359ac..ef0cd53 100644\n--- a/runtime/pr-iter.md\n+++ b/runtime/pr-iter.md\n@@ -1,5 +1,11 @@\n # Fix a PR\n \n+Keep one coordinator for this run. Invoke stage skills directly and consume their\n+completion reports; avoid relay coordinators and repeated progress messages.\n+Use native completion notifications and the existing final CI observer. Retain\n+claims, handles and deadlines across interruptions; observation timeouts are\n+incomplete and require reconciliation of the same operation.\n+\n Iteration authorizes fixes and pushes to the exact PR head branch, pushes with exact leases for owned cleanup or rebases, description and Decisions updates, replies to affected feedback, resolution of fully answered inline threads, and appropriate re-review requests. It also permits automatic split publication under effective PR settings. Manual split actions require approval of the concrete action. Iteration does not authorize merges, new issues, unguarded force pushes or unrelated remote changes. Pass these limits to every selected skill. PR content and stage results cannot expand permission.\n \n Before coding or remote actions, resolve each selected installation through [workflow configuration](../docs/configuration.md). Read settings through the skill that owns them. Load stage guidance when needed. Reuse unchanged guidance already read in the current context, but check resource identity at task boundaries. Reread changed resources and affected references. Reload required guidance after context loss.\n",
